1. `main` rows (WI-mulaj). A pattern can read `Symbol.qualified_name` (new `qualified_name:` filter). Go's row asks for `main.main`, so a `main` of another package is no program start. Haskell's asks for `Main.main` (haskell.py now records the module); 0.90 -> 0.95. The item's Erlang half was wrong: the analyzer names a function `name/arity`, so the row (`main|start`) matched nothing. It is `main/1` now and Erlang takes the unmeasured value.
